WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:07.330
This lesson becomes clearer when before the worked example, separate emf, terminal p.d., and internal resistance instead of treating the battery as an ideal black box.

2
00:00:07.330 --> 00:00:14.660
Full lift means emf: EMF is the total energy supplied per coulomb by the source before any internal loss is removed.

3
00:00:14.660 --> 00:00:21.990
Delivered lift means terminal p.d.: The external circuit receives the terminal p.d., not always the full emf.

4
00:00:21.990 --> 00:00:29.320
Main trap means ideal-source thinking: A real source loses volts internally when current flows, so loaded readings drop.

5
00:00:29.320 --> 00:00:36.650
A real source should be read as emf split into delivered voltage and internal loss.

6
00:00:36.650 --> 00:00:43.980
Keep this takeaway in view: A real source should be read as emf split into delivered voltage and internal loss.

