20
00:02:13.366 --> 00:02:20.040
Loaded circuit: When current flows, the internal resistance steals part of the source lift inside the battery.

21
00:02:20.040 --> 00:02:25.871
The full pressure rise is like emf, and the delivered outlet pressure is like terminal p.d.

22
00:02:25.871 --> 00:02:31.702
That analogy helps because the loss belongs to the source route, not to the measurement instrument.

23
00:02:31.702 --> 00:02:37.532
Pump rise means full source lift: The pump can be thought of as the source giving the full available energy rise.

24
00:02:37.532 --> 00:02:43.363
Internal friction means loss inside: Part of the rise is consumed internally when the flow through the machine increases.

25
00:02:43.363 --> 00:02:49.194
Outlet reading means delivered result: The outlet pressure is like terminal p.d.: it is the delivered remainder, not the whole lift.

26
